<article class="env-lemma" id="0041">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0041">Lemma <span data-tag="0041">4.35.7</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a category. The $2$-category of categories fibred in groupoids over $\mathcal{C}$ has 2-fibre products, and they are described as in Lemma <a href="/tag/0040" data-tag="0040">4.32.3</a>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/02XQ" data-tag="02XQ">4.33.10</a> the fibre product as described in Lemma <a href="/tag/0040" data-tag="0040">4.32.3</a> is a fibred category. Hence it suffices to prove that the fibre categories are groupoids, see Lemma <a href="/tag/003V" data-tag="003V">4.35.2</a>. By Lemma <a href="/tag/02XI" data-tag="02XI">4.32.5</a> it is enough to show that the $2$-fibre product of groupoids is a groupoid, which is clear (from the construction in Lemma <a href="/tag/02X9" data-tag="02X9">4.31.4</a> for example). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>